contentText:
What&#8217;s better than a ticket to Hollywood while competing on American Idol ? Maybe a gift from an American Idol winner herself.

In a Monday (April 13) Facebook post , American Idol season 24 top 11 contestant Hannah Harper shared that she received a personal gift from season four winner and current judge Carrie Underwood .

&#8220;Didn’t think my first piece of Tiffany & Co. jewelry would come from Carrie Underwood,&#8221; wrote Harper, who shared a photo of the iconic Tiffany blue box and something even more special than the jewelry itself. &#8220;But truly, the part that got me the most was the handwritten note. That meant more than anything.&#8221;

Alongside the jewelry, Underwood included a heartfelt note to Harper, praising her talent and congratulating her on making it far in the competition.

&#8220;From the first time I laid eyes on you — and heard your story [and] your voice, I knew you were special,&#8221; Underwood said in the handwritten letter, calling Harper &#8220;an inspiration&#8221; that women and moms everywhere relate to. Harper has opened up about her experiences as a stay-at-home mom, facing postpartum depression and overcoming the harder days of motherhood. &#8220;I [cannot] wait to see what God has in store for you [and] I am so blessed to have a front row seat.&#8221;

In her caption Harper called Underwood a &#8220;good kind human.&#8221; &#8220;Y’all, she’s as down-to-earth and genuine as they come,&#8221; she wrote.

Fellow Top 11 contestant Keyla Richardson also shared her special gift from the &#8220;Before He Cheats&#8221; singer via Instagram on Tuesday (April 14). Like Harper, Richardson received something from Tiffany and Co. and a handwritten note.

&#8220;Your kindness and generosity mean more than words can express,&#8221; Richardson wrote in her caption, thanking Underwood for the present. &#8220;The fact that you took the time to bless someone like that speaks to the incredible woman and class act that you are.&#8221;

Underwood won American Idol in 2005 and now serves as a judge on the current 24th season, her second year in a row in the role. Since her win 21 years ago, the country star has gone on to hit the Billboard Hot 100 43 times and the Billboard 200 10 times.
